DRAFT -- NOT SENT. Prepared for review; do not mail without approval.

Subject: [PATCH] configs/qemu_microblaze*: use the CPU features QEMU provides

QEMU's MicroBlaze CPU model enables the hardware divider, multiplier
and barrel shifter by default (target/microblaze/cpu.c: use-div,
use-hw-mul, use-barrel; the petalogix boards override only version and
endianness), and the kernel's own mmu_defconfig builds for them. The
qemu_microblaze*_mmu defconfigs do neither: the custom linux.config
omits CONFIG_XILINX_MICROBLAZE0_USE_DIV (so it defaults to 0), and the
userland is built with GCC's MicroBlaze defaults -- software multiply,
software divide, no barrel shifter. Disassembly of the shipped ld.so,
libc and busybox shows zero mul, idiv or bsll instructions.

The cost is measurable. Profiling a boot to the login prompt with a
counting TCG plugin (206.8M translation blocks executed, symbolized
against System.map and the built libraries): the dynamic loader alone
spends 7.5M block executions in __umodsi3 -- every ELF symbol-hash
lookup takes a software modulo -- plus soft multiplies, and glibc's
word-at-a-time string code pays for every shift.

With this change (kernel USE_DIV=1; BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION passing
-mno-xl-soft-mul -mno-xl-soft-div -mxl-barrel-shift), the same boot
executes 48.7M non-idle translation blocks instead of 92.6M (-47%):
__umodsi3 and __mulsi3 disappear from the profile, strcmp drops 78%
and the dynamic loader's do_lookup_x 74% from the barrel shifter and
hardware multiply alone. Verified by disassembly of the rebuilt
binaries (ld.so: 25 mul / 39 idivu / 30 bslli, libc: 249 / 271 / 217).

-mxl-pattern-compare was also tested and emitted no pcmpbf
instructions with GCC 15, so it is not included.

Note for users updating an existing build tree: BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION
is baked into the toolchain wrapper when the toolchain is built, so
this change requires a clean build (or a toolchain rebuild) to take
effect on the target packages -- a fresh defconfig build gets it
automatically.

These defconfigs exist to run on QEMU's petalogix machines, which is
what makes the instruction set knowable; nothing here is claimed for
other MicroBlaze hardware. Tested on qemu_microblazeel_mmu (boot to
login, glibc rootfs); the big-endian variant is changed by symmetry.

Signed-off-by: Sam Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/board/qemu/microblazebe-mmu/linux.config b/board/qemu/microblazebe-mmu/linux.config
index 7bcd3820..b3c85fcf 100644
--- a/board/qemu/microblazebe-mmu/linux.config
+++ b/board/qemu/microblazebe-mmu/linux.config
@@ -18,3 +18,4 @@ CONFIG_SERIAL_UARTLITE=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_UARTLITE_CONSOLE=y
 # CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE is not set
 CONFIG_TMPFS=y
+CONFIG_XILINX_MICROBLAZE0_USE_DIV=1
diff --git a/board/qemu/microblazeel-mmu/linux.config b/board/qemu/microblazeel-mmu/linux.config
index a6228280..6d7fb51c 100644
--- a/board/qemu/microblazeel-mmu/linux.config
+++ b/board/qemu/microblazeel-mmu/linux.config
@@ -17,3 +17,4 @@ CONFIG_SERIAL_UARTLITE=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_UARTLITE_CONSOLE=y
 # CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE is not set
 CONFIG_TMPFS=y
+CONFIG_XILINX_MICROBLAZE0_USE_DIV=1
diff --git a/configs/qemu_microblazebe_mmu_defconfig b/configs/qemu_microblazebe_mmu_defconfig
index cc6871e2..3d890609 100644
--- a/configs/qemu_microblazebe_mmu_defconfig
+++ b/configs/qemu_microblazebe_mmu_defconfig
@@ -16,3 +16,4 @@ BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_INITRAMFS=y
 # BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_TAR is not set
 BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_QEMU=y
 BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_QEMU_SYSTEM_MODE=y
+BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION="-mno-xl-soft-mul -mno-xl-soft-div -mxl-barrel-shift"
diff --git a/configs/qemu_microblazeel_mmu_defconfig b/configs/qemu_microblazeel_mmu_defconfig
index 8945a775..559a9750 100644
--- a/configs/qemu_microblazeel_mmu_defconfig
+++ b/configs/qemu_microblazeel_mmu_defconfig
@@ -16,3 +16,4 @@ BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_INITRAMFS=y
 # BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_TAR is not set
 BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_QEMU=y
 BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_QEMU_SYSTEM_MODE=y
+BR2_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION="-mno-xl-soft-mul -mno-xl-soft-div -mxl-barrel-shift"
